{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not take a widow's garment in pledge.</b> Scripture already warned the lender not to enter the borrower's house to take a pledge from him — that is what it said, ״לא תבא אל ביתו״ and so forth — all the more so if she is a widow. Rather, it is to transgress thereby two negative commandments, for her tears are ever-present and her spirit is lowly, and the Torah warned concerning her in several places. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: even the widow of a king."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:52.203630506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}